1. **Linear Fenwick Tree Initialization**: The initial insertion of all elements into the Fenwick tree can be done in $O(N)$ time instead of $O(N \log N)$.
2. **Inlining Functions**: Function call overhead in Python can be significant in tight loops. Inlining the Fenwick tree `query` and `update` logic directly inside the main loop will provide a noticeable speedup. 
